# November 19, 2026: southwestern Idaho. The Boise Basin gold camps (Idaho City and Placerville, Boise County), Boise
# itself (Ada County), and the Snake River and Owyhee country south of it (Swan Falls, the Guffey bridge, Silver City,
# Oreana, Wickahoney). Region drawn at random by tools/choose.py (id).
# Sources read in this session: National Register nomination forms (NPGallery "_text" PDFs, read with tools/page.py),
# Wikipedia articles (tools/wiki_raw.py), HMdb.org marker pages, the Idaho State Historical Society's Old Pen page, the
# City of Boise's Boise Depot pages, Idaho Power's Swan Falls pages, the BLM's Swan Falls, Celebration Park and Silver
# City Campground pages and Owyhee byway guide, the parish page for St. Joseph's, the Idaho Heritage Trust's Guffey
# Bridge page and the IDGenWeb Idaho City cemetery page. No interior was seen by any source opened unless the entry says so.
